;; Models that refuse a sampling parameter every request would otherwise carry
;; (byj-gly.369). A RESOURCE, not code (RFC-001): a vendor deprecating one is
;; a fact about its models, and saying so should not need a rebuild.
;;
;; :no-temperature — model ids, as regexes found anywhere in the id, that
;; answer any temperature with a validation error; a request to one leaves
;; temperature out (llm/takes-temperature?). Measured on Bedrock
;; (us-east-1, 2026-10-17) with temperature 0:
;;   refused  claude-opus-4-7, opus-4-8, opus-5, sonnet-5, opus-5-5, sonnet-5-5,
;;            haiku-5-5 — "`temperature` is deprecated for this model";
;;            gpt-5.6-sol — "This model doesn't support the temperature field"
;;   accepted claude-opus-4-5, opus-4-6, sonnet-4-5, sonnet-4-6, haiku-4-5,
;;            gpt-oss-120b
;; Fable 5 and 5.1 failed first on their data retention mode, so are listed
;; with the 5.x family they belong to, not measured.
{:no-temperature ["claude-(opus|sonnet|haiku|fable)-(4-[7-9]|5)"
                  "gpt-5\\.6"]}
